  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mwika Kinyamvuo Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture. Export Crop - Coffee Beneficiaries: 910 small holder coffee farmers, of which 250 are women Project Description: The capacity building grant will assist Mwika Kinyamvuo Agriculture and Marketing Cooperative Society to plant improved higher yielding coffee varieties and earn increased incomes. The grant will assist the farmers to form a more organized Value Chain for production, processing and marketing of organic coffee through training in agronomic skills, financial management skills so that they are able to control their financial transactions so as to enhance transparency and accountability. The farmers will use the grant to access training in governance to ensure members are empowered to understand and know their role as key stakeholders of the cooperative. At processing level, the grant will assist the cooperative to complete the installation of new coffee processing equipment. The grant will assist farmers to develop a business plan have access to crop finance so that they receive advance cash payments upon delivery of their coffee to the cooperative.</narrative>
  </description>
